{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Root cause, 2026-11-12 ~15:10 PST (read-only; figures kept in operator-local notes outside the repo; ratios only here).\nObservation:\n- The \"about 3x\" at 05:40 PST compared the cap's metered estimate with Cost Explorer's SAME-DAY figure. Re-read at 15:04 PST, Cost Explorer for 2026-11-12 had risen about 60%, and the ratio is now 1.94 (the metered value is frozen since the deny attached). Most of the 3x was Cost Explorer lag, not estimate error.\n- 2026-11-11, which Cost Explorer has fully settled (recomputing the day from per-ModelId token counts at the per-usage-type billed rates matches Cost Explorer within 1%), ran at 2.04, above the README's documented 1.1–1.9 band.\n- Cost Explorer's per-usage-type rates for the 5.5 models are lower than the 4.x rates the CEILING table was derived from (2026-09-25). For Opus 5.5 the ceiling is 1.56x the billed input, output and cache-write rates and 3.125x the billed cache-read rate; cache reads are about 90% of tokens on both days, and Opus 5.5 carries about 90% of the traffic.\nConclusion: the estimate is still an upper bound (correct direction) but runs about 2x for the 5.5 generation, because the ceilings remain tied to the 4.x price list (4.x models are still inside the 60-day derivation window) and cache reads dominate the token volume. The README band reflects the 4.x mix.\nFix options (operator decision, returned to the coordinator): (a) update the README band and its explanation only, keeping the accepted early-trip posture; (b) implement the README's own reserved remedy, an exact-match per-ModelId rate table that defaults to the ceiling (applied as a discount only for series that were read, so a missing read falls back to the ceiling), which would bring the 5.5 ratio near 1.25 but puts per-model unit rates in the public repo and lowers the safety margin."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1794524744581832590,"uuid":"d8c5720c-9386-4998-af30-b812b22a7cfc"}